From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:53:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] flashnext: small decode tiles, preallocated prompt
 pool, MoE router glue, beside packing, fixes

Small-row decode tiles, late n-gram hints, a preallocated startup plan, the decode router front in one launch, a
recall free-space floor, pshare beside the shared pool at --tp 2, skipping DeltaNet end states for short drafted
windows (TF_FLASHNEXT_LATE_SKIP), packing a second waiting prompt's piece beside a pass, and fixes to beside pieces
at join and shutdown.

TF_FLASHNEXT_LATE_SKIP is ported from the idea in Picom-code's pico-dgx-qwen38 patch 0111
(q38-drafted-windows-skip-deltanet-end-state-writes, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/Picom-code/pico-dgx-qwen38), which
builds on TensorFold (Apache-2.0) and MiaAI-Lab's single-Spark recipe (MIT); rewritten for this tree's lane kernels
and late-row log, no code copied.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_DEC_SMALL, small-row decode tiles with the same bytes (default off)
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_HINT_LATE holds a shared round's first n-gram read hints until the head's first pass
  is queued
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_POOL: preallocate the startup plan and carve later device buffers from it
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MOE_GLUE fuses the decode router front into one launch
- fix(recall): --recall-min-free-gib sets the record's free-space floor; GET /v1/recall says waiting
- flashnext-draft-hint-late: a round's rows fit the rank frame limit at 24 streams; rank 1 starts with no head
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_SHARE serves beside TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_POOL at --tp 2
- test(flashnext): the lane-backend GPU tests attach TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARED_POOL as the host does
- test(flashnext): the ride test reports a whole resumed prompt's unseen inner cut instead of failing
- fix(flashnext): beside on, a second read waits instead of riding, and only alone rows owe decode debt
- fix(flashnext): beside on, a lane that opens while a piece is beside joins it first when the lanes' map would grow
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_LATE_SKIP, a short drafted window writes no DeltaNet end states
- fix(flashnext): beside on, closing the engine joins a piece beside before any lane or rank sequence is freed
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_PACK, a beside pass takes a second waiting whole prompt's piece
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_PACK_ANY packs beside pieces of any size; FP8MMA keeps the gather ahead

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DEC_SMALL: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_DEC_SMALL, small-row decode tiles with the same bytes
  (default off)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_HINT_LATE is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and sets no tp_flags bit
- TF_FLASHNEXT_LATE_SKIP is off unset or 0, 2 to 48 pending rows as given, refuses anything else and sets no tp_flags
  bit
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_PACK is off unset or 0, takes 64-row steps from 128 to the widest chunk, refuses anything
  else, and needs the beside lane, its scratch and two pieces' rows
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_PACK_ANY is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, and needs
  TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_PACK
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MOE_GLUE is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and leaves the identity bits alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_POOL=1 (rank-local, set it on both) preallocates, once the startup plan is made, each rank's
  planned bytes (its streams' full-window charge and the prompt cache's budget, at most TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_POOL_GIB
  GiB when set) in 4 GiB chunks...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_POOL_GIB=<GiB> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_POOL): bounds the preallocated pool past the startup
  plan.
